## UI Component Reuse

Before building any UI element (confirmation dialogs, toasts, inline prompts, etc.),
**check `frontend/src/components/ui/` first** for a reusable component that fits the need.
If one exists, use it — do not inline the same UI pattern.

If no reusable component exists and the UI pattern is likely to appear in other parts of the
app, **extract it as a new component in `frontend/src/components/ui/`** rather than embedding
it inline. Every component in `ui/` must:

1. Have `"use client"` at the top.
2. Export a named function component (no default exports).
3. Define a TypeScript interface for its props, exported alongside the component.
4. Use CSS custom-property tokens only — never hex, rgba, or named colors.
5. Reference constants from `@/utils/constants.ts` for sizing, radius, spacing.
6. Include a JSDoc comment with a `Usage:` example.

When in doubt, look at existing components (`CheckboxField.tsx`, `Notice.tsx`, `ConfirmDialog.tsx`)
for the pattern.

